            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\r\n\r\nDoing that in built-in way would require another operator mapping which is a bit too much. Besides that, this can be achieved by tweaking [`config.sort.func`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/b1af49d98233180c6045e81f4aef5b663d032b62/doc/mini-operators.txt#L215). For example, by toggling it between `nil` (default, ascending) and something like `function(content) return MiniOperators.default_sort_func(content, { compare_fun = function(a, b) return a > b end }) end`.",
